🔷 1. VM (Virtual Machine) OS / Platform Upgrade
✅ What is upgraded?
OS image (Ubuntu → newer version)
Patching (security updates)
VM size / disk

🔧 How upgrade happens
✅ Case 1: In-place OS update (minor updates)
Inside VM:
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade
👉 Terraform NOT involved
👉 OS patched manually or via automation (Azure Update Manager)

✅ Case 2: Recreate VM (Image change)
Terraform:
Terraformsource_image_reference {  publisher = "Canonical"  offer     = "UbuntuServer"  sku       = "20_04-lts"   # changed to 22_04}``Show more lines
Plan:
-/+ azurerm_linux_virtual_machine
(forces replacement)


🚀 Real Production Approach
❌ Don’t recreate directly (downtime)
✅ Use Rolling / Blue-Green
✔️ Enterprise way:

Create new VM with new OS
Attach to Load Balancer
Shift traffic gradually
Delete old VM


🔷 2. AKS (Kubernetes) Upgrade
✅ What is upgraded?

Kubernetes version
Node OS image
Node pools


🔧 How upgrade happens
Terraform:
Terraformresource "azurerm_kubernetes_cluster" "aks" {  kubernetes_version = "1.29.0"}Show more lines

🚀 What Azure DOES internally
✅ AKS performs rolling upgrade automatically
Steps:

Add new node with new version
Drain old node (evict pods)
Move pods to new node
Delete old node


✅ Zero Downtime (if app is configured correctly)
Requirements:

Multiple replicas (pods)
PodDisruptionBudget
Readiness/Liveness probes


⚠️ Risk if not configured

Single pod app → downtime
No health checks → failures


🔷 3. App Service Upgrade
✅ What is upgraded?

Runtime (Node, .NET, Java)
App Service Plan SKU
OS (Windows/Linux)


🔧 Terraform Example
Terraformsite_config {  linux_fx_version = "NODE|18-lts"}Show more lines

🚀 How upgrade happens
✅ In-place (default)

App restarts
New runtime applied


✅ Production method: Deployment Slots
👉 This is VERY important in enterprise
Steps:

Create staging slot
Deploy new version there
Test application
Swap slots

Shellaz webapp deployment slot swap``Show more lines
✅ Result:
ZERO downtime

Resource    UpgradeType        Strategy
VM          OS / image         Recreate + Rolling
AKS         Version /node      Rolling (automatic)
App Service  Runtime           In-place / Slot swap
